<title>ITALY: Italy express train derails, deaths feared.</title>
<headline>Italy express train derails, deaths feared.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Milan-Rome express train derailed on Sunday near the station at the northern city of Piacenza and a number of people were feared dead, the Italian news agency Ansa reported.  </p>
<p>Ansa said the train was a Rome-bound Pendolino, a highly popular fast train that makes the run between Italy's two most important cities in just over four hours.</p>
<p>The report said a number of carriages of the train were involved in the derailment and many ambulances and rescue vechicles were converging on the scene.</p>
</text>
